            <ArticleTitle>Primary benign ulcer of the gall bladder.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>321-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>It is sometimes impossible to come to a final diagnosis in patients with dyspepsia and upper abdominal pain in spite of extensive investigation. Such patients are usually given vague diagnoses like &quot;non-ulcer dyspepsia&quot; and they represent an important diagnostic challenge.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
